You have two interfaces:
```ts
interface Named { name: string; }
interface Aged { age: number; }
```
Which declaration creates a new interface `Person` containing both properties using interface inheritance?

Consider the following type aliases:
```ts
type ResponseA = { status: string; data: object };
type ResponseB = { status: number; message: string };
type CombinedResponse = ResponseA & ResponseB;
```
What is the type of `CombinedResponse['status']`?
